# SDEMO-T02: Railway Deploy

## Objective

Deploy work-control to Railway. Get a public URL. WebSocket must work.

## Prerequisites

- SDEMO-T01 CLOSED (build passes, node-server preset)
- Railway account (railway.app) — free tier sufficient

## App-agent preflight

- [ ] MCP preflight §2
- [ ] Confirm T01 `.output/` is clean Node build

## Implementation

### 1. Install Railway CLI

```bash
npm i -g @railway/cli
railway login
```

### 2. Create `railway.json` in repo root (or `apps/work-control/`)

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://railway.app/railway.schema.json",
  "build": {
    "builder": "NIXPACKS",
    "buildCommand": "bun install && bun run build --filter=@app-agent/work-control"
  },
  "deploy": {
    "startCommand": "node apps/work-control/.output/server/index.mjs",
    "healthcheckPath": "/api/health",
    "restartPolicyType": "ON_FAILURE"
  }
}
```

### 3. Create `.env` for Railway (set via Railway dashboard, not committed)

Required env vars:
```
NUXT_SESSION_PASSWORD=<random 32+ char string>
PORT=3003
NODE_ENV=production
# LLM agents (optional — mock agent works without these)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...
```

Do NOT set `CORE_DATASOURCE_*` — defaults to SQLite (fine for demo).

### 4. Deploy

```bash
cd /Users/denistka/Projects/app-agent-io/DAWWWB-app-agent
railway init          # link to project
railway up            # deploy
railway domain        # get public URL
```

### 5. Verify WebSocket

Open public URL → work-control loads → chat → type message → ROOT responds.
Check browser DevTools WS tab: `wss://<project>.railway.app` connection stays open.

### 6. SQLite persistence note

SQLite file lives in Railway ephemeral filesystem. Data resets on restart/redeploy.
**This is acceptable for demo.** Document this for the audience.

## Done when

- [ ] Public URL loads work-control without error
- [ ] Chat flow works: type → ROOT responds (mock or LLM)
- [ ] Board loads, tasks run
- [ ] WS connection stays alive (no reconnect loop in DevTools)
- [ ] URL shared to Denis — accessible from another browser without login
